{"summary": "Here is a JSON representation of the text:

```
{
  "title": "Update EU database of processing factors",
  "abstract": "This report presents an update of the European Union (EU) database of processing factors for pesticide residues in food. The database was extended with respect to considered processes and processed commodities, while some commodities were not included due to their composite nature or edible peel.",
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "text": "Establish a mechanism for regular updates of the EU database of processing factors",
      "description": "New studies are conducted and submitted continuously, and residue definitions keep changing."
    },
    {
      "text": "Align raw commodity categories used with respect to storage stability and analytical methods",
      "description": "This should be kept in mind when updating the respective OECD guideline and guidance document."
    },
    {
      "text": "Improve transparency and traceability of processing studies underlying a PF",
      "description": "Unambiguous study citations (title, author, year, study number) were often missing for processing studies evaluated in EFSA’s Reasoned Opinions and in the underlying Evaluation Reports."
    }
  ],
  "database_extension": [
    {
      "text": "Added new processing studies to the existing data pool",
      "description": "The database was extended with respect to considered processes and processed commodities, while some commodities were not included due to their composite nature or edible peel."
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased database quality",
      "description": "The update provided a broader and more robust set of processing factors."
    }
  ],
  "future_work": [
    {
      "text": "Establish a set of quality criteria for generic drying factors",
      "description": "A list of suitable factors should be provided together with recommendations for extrapolation."
    },
    {
      "text": "Explore the use of physico-chemical properties of active substances to allow for comparison and extrapolation to other compounds",
      "description": "This could provide a valuable source of real-world processing factors, beyond laboratory-scale experiments."
    }
  ]
}
```

Note that this is not an exhaustive representation of all the information in the text. I have only extracted the main points and recommendations mentioned in the abstract and conclusions sections.", "dataset_name": "European database of processing factors for pesticides residues in food", "source_length": 74618, "full_source_length": 70953, "num_context_blocks": 1, "extraction_strategy": "keyword"}

